<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sao Shwe Thaike</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896–1962</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sao Shwe Thaike was the saopha of Yawnghwe, a Shan state on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inle-lake">Inle Lake</a>, and the first President of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1948 to 1952. A leading figure among the Shan princes at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panglong-conference">Panglong Conference</a> of 1947, he helped bring the Shan states into the union. After the military coup of 1962 he was arrested and died in prison that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sao-shwe-thaike.jpg" alt="Sao Shwe Thaike" width="220" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sao_Shwe_Thaik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
